{
  "name": "site-membership-parity",
  "note": "Admit two people, grant the first an open-ended admin role and the second a windowed one, then disable and delete the second. Five refusals ride along: the last open-ended admin may not take an end date, a window past 365 days, an admin disabling themselves, enabling a deleted person, and deleting a person who is not disabled. A runtime that accepts any of them is the failure worth catching.",
